  "title": "Mendaña's voyage to the Solomon Islands",
  "summary": "Álvaro de Mendaña sailed from Callao, Peru, in November 1567 with a Spanish expedition and reached Santa Isabel in the Solomon Islands on 7 February 1568. The Spanish explored Guadalcanal and San Cristóbal, where their attempt to settle failed, and in the summer of 1568 began the long voyage back toward Peru.",
  "when": {
    "start": {
      "year": 1567
    },
    "end": {
      "year": 1568
    },
    "precision": "month",
    "uncertainty": {
      "note": "The Solomon Islands Historical Encyclopaedia gives November 1567 for departure (no day), 23 January for Ontong Java, 7 February 1568 for Santa Isabel and early August 1568 for the departure north. Encyclopedia.com gives only 'late 1567' and 'summer 1568'. The encyclopaedia says the expedition reached either Nui or part of the Ellice Group before Ontong Java; that stop is not plotted."
    },
